From d72f1a73a685e50c071043cc3f62769e369f49a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Phase 2 part 1: communications foundation and unified
 inbox

Database (supabase/migrations/20261007120000_phase2_communications.sql)
- provider_accounts per organization (Telnyx, Twilio, Resend); a number
  belongs to one organization; credentials ciphertext hidden from the
  Data API and released only by provider_secret() to members+
- conversations and messages with a trigger-enforced status machine
  (no forged inbound, no fake receipts, no edits after sending), every
  message on the contact timeline, unread counts maintained
- suppressions written only via apply_opt_out / clear_opt_out (START from
  the person or an admin), audited; webhook_events for idempotency
- 31 new SQL security tests (85 total)

Application
- APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY vault for provider credentials (separate from the
  DB secret, key-id mismatch detection)
- compliance gate on every send: consent, opt-outs, do-not-contact,
  quiet hours in the business time zone, marketing opt-out text, length;
  re-applied when scheduled messages are dispatched
- provider adapters with send, credential test, and webhook signature
  verification (Telnyx ed25519, Twilio HMAC); failover across numbers on
  temporary errors only
- verified webhooks for replies, delivery receipts and STOP/START;
  scheduled dispatch via the existing scheduler
- AI operator tools: list_conversations, get_conversation, send_message
  (Messages permission; the gate still applies after approval)
- Conversations (unified inbox) and Channels pages; Text/Email buttons on
  contacts; navigation entries
- 45 new unit tests (128 total)

